# Folders exposed to the Hermes agent, beyond projects/. Copy to `etc/mounts`
# (gitignored) or, better, let amphoractl write it:
#
#     ./bin/amphoractl mount add ~/Documents/Research
#     ./bin/amphoractl mount add ~/Media/Reference refs --ro
#     ./bin/amphoractl mount ls
#     ./bin/amphoractl up               # dind holds the bind; it is fixed at create time
#
# One entry per line: name<TAB>path[<TAB>ro]. Read as data, never sourced as shell —
# a leading ~/ is expanded and nothing else is, so no variables, no globs, no commands.
# Spaces work as separators, but a path containing spaces needs the tabs.
#
# Each entry reaches the agent at /mounts/<name>, at the same path inside amphora-dind.
# The names kanban and outbox are taken. The path must exist and must be inside a
# folder the podman machine shares, or it binds as an empty directory with no error
# anywhere — `amphoractl shares` lists what the machine needs.
#
# amphoractl refuses a source that would expose the stack itself, the snapshots in
# backups/, the outbox, your whole home directory, or the Obsidian vault beyond its
# Kanban folder.
# Everything else on the Mac stays invisible to the agent, which is the default.
#
#name	path	[ro]
#research	/Users/you/Documents/Research
#refs	/Users/you/Media/Reference	ro
